# Line-ending policy (the R487 re-audit hardening finding)
#
# The engine's hash-pinned tamper-evidence (DIGESTS.json sha256 pins,
# freeze-check corpus hashes, envelope hashes) cannot survive a
# default Windows checkout: core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF -> CRLF in
# the working tree and every pinned digest stops matching. Forcing LF
# on the pinned text types makes the tamper-evidence semantics hold
# on every platform. The tree is pure LF (verified 2026-09-17: zero
# tracked files carry CRLF), so this attribute set changes no
# committed bytes â€” it only constrains future checkouts.
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
